==English==

===Etymology===
{{suffix|serious|ly|lang=en}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|US}} {{IPA|/ˈsɪɹiəsli/|/ˈsiɹiəsli/|lang=en}}
* {{audio|en-us-seriously.ogg|Audio (US)|lang=en}}

===Adverb===
{{en-adv}}

# {{label|en|manner}} In a [[serious]] or [[literal]] manner.
#: ''He was hoping that we would take him '''seriously'''.''
#: ''Jimmy [[joking|jokingly]] called Bob a [[doofus]]. Bob took the insult '''seriously'''.
# {{label|en|speech act}} {{non-gloss definition|Used to attempt to introduce a serious point in a less serious conversation}}
#: ''Now, '''seriously''', why did you forget to feed the cat today?''
# {{label|en|speech act}} {{non-gloss definition|Used to call back to a previous point, either in [[disbelief]] or [[emphasis]]}}
#: ''You baked 10 cakes. '''Seriously''', why did you do that?''

